WEBVTT

00:00:09.940 --> 00:00:15.750
Full energy is troubled because there's no place to go

00:00:16.210 --> 00:00:22.030
A slight shake destroys boredom

00:00:22.320 --> 00:00:28.170
I Ride, On the White Line  OH, OH, OH

00:00:28.420 --> 00:00:34.240
Sit Down  At the place I trust  OH, OH, OH

00:00:34.430 --> 00:00:37.540
We can go even if we're lost

00:00:37.770 --> 00:00:43.650
Everyone receives freedom and passion

00:00:44.040 --> 00:00:49.850
We were born to shine, and our journey continues

00:00:50.180 --> 00:00:56.060
Your soul is the key that supports our uncertain days

00:00:56.350 --> 00:01:02.000
The best growth creates an unstoppable WILD DRIVE

00:01:02.420 --> 00:01:08.270
We still quietly knock on the door

00:01:21.200 --> 00:01:23.860
Swords of Revealing Light's effect is over!

00:01:23.860 --> 00:01:25.230
Get ready!

00:01:28.450 --> 00:01:32.140
I can hear God's pulse from my deck.

00:01:34.020 --> 00:01:34.970
I draw!

00:01:39.130 --> 00:01:40.850
God is in my hand!

00:01:41.170 --> 00:01:42.310
Obelisk...

00:01:43.170 --> 00:01:46.420
Des Feral Imp!  Attack her directly!

00:01:51.910 --> 00:01:53.510
The future is infinite!

00:01:53.510 --> 00:01:56.220
The past is nothing more than a set of footprints!

00:01:56.220 --> 00:01:59.970
The past means nothing to me!

00:01:59.970 --> 00:02:04.340
Including the moment when you gave me the God Card, Ishizu!

00:02:04.720 --> 00:02:08.570
But God will not lead you to victory.

00:02:09.700 --> 00:02:11.710
Listen, Ishizu!

00:02:11.710 --> 00:02:14.500
The future doesn't guide me!

00:02:14.500 --> 00:02:18.300
The road that I take becomes the future!

00:02:20.280 --> 00:02:26.290
The Strike That Changes the Future

00:02:34.020 --> 00:02:38.200
Ishizu, remember that I didn't choose the God.

00:02:39.080 --> 00:02:40.740
God chose me.

00:02:40.940 --> 00:02:43.770
No, you weren't chosen.

00:02:43.770 --> 00:02:47.800
Obelisk will lead you to defeat.

00:02:48.280 --> 00:02:53.250
Even though she's in big trouble, she doesn't look worried.

00:02:53.460 --> 00:02:57.050
Is she calm because she actually saw the future?

00:02:57.050 --> 00:02:58.690
That's impossible!

00:02:59.020 --> 00:03:01.490
I don't understand Ishizu's strategy.

00:03:01.760 --> 00:03:05.820
Her main cards are in the graveyard.

00:03:06.130 --> 00:03:07.110
Graveyard...

00:03:10.710 --> 00:03:16.040
If Marik and Ishizu are siblings, Ishizu is also a gravekeeper.

00:03:16.640 --> 00:03:19.260
Keep the grave...  Keep...

00:03:20.510 --> 00:03:24.600
Does this keyword hold the secret to Ishizu's deck?

00:03:25.460 --> 00:03:28.190
I'll corner you further this turn.

00:03:29.660 --> 00:03:35.560
Kaiba is digging his own grave, so he'll suffer even more.

00:03:46.750 --> 00:03:47.970
Here I go!

00:03:47.970 --> 00:03:49.710
I flip over my set card!

00:03:49.930 --> 00:03:52.640
Virus Cannon activates!

00:03:54.330 --> 00:03:55.400
No way!

00:03:58.130 --> 00:04:00.760
Send her spell cards to her graveyard!

00:04:08.300 --> 00:04:13.730
Ishizu, select ten spell cards in your deck and send them to the graveyard.

00:04:15.520 --> 00:04:18.340
Your deck is completely destroyed.

00:04:18.340 --> 00:04:23.910
You no longer have enough monster or spell cards to have a decent duel.

00:04:27.500 --> 00:04:30.800
You still think I'm destined to lose?

00:04:31.700 --> 00:04:34.240
Nothing has changed.

00:04:34.240 --> 00:04:36.520
I predicted this would happen.

00:04:36.520 --> 00:04:37.640
What?

00:04:37.640 --> 00:04:40.060
Still acting tough?

00:04:41.350 --> 00:04:43.530
You're the one who fell for a trap.

00:04:43.530 --> 00:04:44.860
A gravekeeper's trap.

00:04:44.860 --> 00:04:45.860
What?

00:04:45.860 --> 00:04:47.800
A gravekeeper's trap?

00:04:48.040 --> 00:04:50.160
I'll show you.

00:04:50.600 --> 00:04:52.000
I flip over my card!

00:04:53.360 --> 00:04:57.240
The trap card Exchange of the Spirit activates!

00:04:57.460 --> 00:04:59.680
Exchange of the Spirit?

00:04:59.680 --> 00:05:06.120
By paying 1000 life points, the cards in our graveyards swap with our decks.

00:05:06.600 --> 00:05:10.020
The cards in our graveyards swap with our decks?

00:05:19.550 --> 00:05:21.730
It's proceeding smoothly.

00:05:22.930 --> 00:05:24.900
No way!  My brother is...

00:05:25.260 --> 00:05:27.340
Damn!  Big bro!

00:05:28.000 --> 00:05:30.270
This was Ishizu's strategy.

00:05:30.640 --> 00:05:34.710
Kaiba's deck dies while Ishizu's deck revives.

00:05:34.920 --> 00:05:39.150
This is why Ishizu kept sending cards to her graveyard.

00:05:39.440 --> 00:05:40.920
How scary.

00:05:40.920 --> 00:05:42.590
Understand now, Kaiba?

00:05:42.900 --> 00:05:46.520
You're the one whose deck is destroyed.

00:05:46.900 --> 00:05:52.000
Since Kaiba destroyed Ishizu's deck, her graveyard is full of cards.

00:05:52.000 --> 00:05:55.900
And most of the cards are her main ones.

00:05:57.570 --> 00:06:01.720
On the other hand, Kaiba only has six cards in his graveyard.

00:06:02.400 --> 00:06:06.110
When he's unable to draw on his 7th turn, he'll lose.

00:06:06.400 --> 00:06:08.050
My turn.

00:06:08.840 --> 00:06:10.210
You...

00:06:10.210 --> 00:06:11.900
I draw a card.

00:06:11.900 --> 00:06:13.760
I summon Kelbek.

00:06:19.360 --> 00:06:21.120
It's over for Kaiba.

00:06:21.360 --> 00:06:24.200
He can't win with only six cards.

00:06:24.200 --> 00:06:27.480
Ishizu really did see the future.

00:06:27.480 --> 00:06:29.530
Or this wouldn't have happened.

00:06:29.980 --> 00:06:30.960
Kaiba...

00:06:31.200 --> 00:06:35.910
I'll never believe that I'll lose!

00:06:36.480 --> 00:06:39.120
I set one card.

00:06:39.380 --> 00:06:40.850
I end my turn.

00:06:45.020 --> 00:06:46.400
Big brother!

00:06:46.400 --> 00:06:47.150
Mokuba!

00:06:48.190 --> 00:06:49.410
Big brother!

00:06:49.410 --> 00:06:52.590
Mokuba, did you finish analyzing the card?

00:06:52.800 --> 00:06:56.360
Not yet.  I was worried about you.

00:06:58.460 --> 00:06:59.530
My turn!

00:07:01.240 --> 00:07:04.280
That card is Virus Cannon.

00:07:06.860 --> 00:07:09.200
I'm not guessing.

00:07:09.200 --> 00:07:11.840
I've already experienced this future.

00:07:12.140 --> 00:07:14.810
You can use that card anyway you like.

00:07:14.810 --> 00:07:16.110
Of course I can!

00:07:16.110 --> 00:07:18.370
Virus Cannon!

00:07:21.450 --> 00:07:23.950
My Counter Trap activates.

00:07:25.480 --> 00:07:27.330
The trap card Null and Void!

00:07:27.850 --> 00:07:29.760
Discard Virus Cannon.

00:07:31.670 --> 00:07:33.970
She knows my entire deck.

00:07:33.970 --> 00:07:34.980
Big brother...

00:07:34.980 --> 00:07:35.700
Kaiba...

00:07:36.170 --> 00:07:38.700
Your next card will be Crush Card Virus.

00:07:38.700 --> 00:07:41.370
But I won't let you add it to your hand.

00:07:41.620 --> 00:07:43.200
You...

00:07:43.550 --> 00:07:44.810
I end my turn.

00:07:45.020 --> 00:07:50.500
Kaiba's Des Feral Imp has more attack points than Ishizu's monster.

00:07:50.500 --> 00:07:52.500
Why didn't he attack, Yugi?

00:07:52.720 --> 00:07:55.300
Kaiba wants to summon Obelisk.

00:07:55.960 --> 00:07:56.820
Say what?

00:07:57.160 --> 00:07:58.250
The God Card?

00:07:58.710 --> 00:08:01.930
It means he has that card in his hand.

00:08:01.930 --> 00:08:05.880
If she gets three monsters on her field...

00:08:06.250 --> 00:08:11.300
Seto, I know you have only one option left.

00:08:11.650 --> 00:08:14.740
The spell card Soul Exchange.

00:08:15.160 --> 00:08:19.410
You're waiting for me to get three monsters on my field.

00:08:19.960 --> 00:08:25.000
In order to summon Obelisk the Tormentor, the God that will lead you to defeat.

00:08:25.500 --> 00:08:28.100
My turn!  I draw!

00:08:28.100 --> 00:08:29.050
I summon Zolga!

00:08:36.500 --> 00:08:38.860
This will lead to your defeat.

00:08:39.560 --> 00:08:42.300
Seto, you have no way to win.

00:08:42.580 --> 00:08:46.060
Can she actually see the future?

00:08:46.400 --> 00:08:49.060
Has she seen my defeat?

00:08:49.600 --> 00:08:50.270
Kaiba!

00:08:52.100 --> 00:08:53.410
I can see it!

00:08:53.980 --> 00:08:54.780
Yugi?

00:08:55.090 --> 00:08:58.210
I see our road of battle that leads forever!

00:08:58.640 --> 00:09:01.150
Use your cards to create your future!

00:09:01.500 --> 00:09:03.090
That's what a duelist does!

00:09:03.410 --> 00:09:08.020
I see a future where we fight in Battle City!

00:09:12.620 --> 00:09:14.960
Then wait for me, Yugi!

00:09:14.960 --> 00:09:17.400
My turn isn't over.

00:09:17.730 --> 00:09:20.080
Zolga attacks Des Feral Imp!

00:09:20.900 --> 00:09:22.370
Destruction Wind Cape!

00:09:22.820 --> 00:09:24.860
Des Feral Imp is destroyed!

00:09:28.220 --> 00:09:31.480
Kelbek attacks you directly!

00:09:35.200 --> 00:09:36.530
How dare you!

00:09:37.920 --> 00:09:41.520
I set a card and end my turn.

00:09:41.980 --> 00:09:47.300
Ishizu's set card is likely a trap that will destroy Crush Card Virus.

00:09:47.720 --> 00:09:50.470
I know it's a trap, but I still have to go for it.

00:09:50.680 --> 00:09:52.060
How humiliating.

00:09:52.060 --> 00:09:55.600
But my Obelisk will crush you to get my revenge!

00:09:57.800 --> 00:09:58.980
My turn!

00:09:59.330 --> 00:10:00.180
I draw!

00:10:00.400 --> 00:10:03.300
I activate the trap card Null and Void!

00:10:04.770 --> 00:10:05.550
I knew it.

00:10:07.740 --> 00:10:10.590
She's blocking Kaiba's every move.

00:10:10.800 --> 00:10:13.840
Ishizu knows what's in his deck.

00:10:14.060 --> 00:10:16.190
He's in a no-win situation.

00:10:16.520 --> 00:10:19.490
Kaiba, don't give up on your future!

00:10:19.880 --> 00:10:22.740
There's no way my brother will lose!

00:10:22.740 --> 00:10:25.870
I believe that you'll win!

00:10:26.750 --> 00:10:27.840
Mokuba...

00:10:28.870 --> 00:10:30.310
Soul Exchange.

00:10:30.780 --> 00:10:36.000
Both players can tribute their opponent's monsters.

00:10:36.820 --> 00:10:39.310
Ishizu has two monsters.

00:10:39.640 --> 00:10:43.040
When she summons a third next turn...

00:10:43.930 --> 00:10:47.440
...Soul Exchange will bring Obelisk!

00:10:48.640 --> 00:10:50.300
I set a card!

00:10:51.220 --> 00:10:52.660
I end my turn!

00:10:52.880 --> 00:10:55.900
Kaiba has no monsters to defend with.

00:10:55.900 --> 00:10:58.670
Ishizu's next attack will finish him!

00:10:58.940 --> 00:11:02.740
His set card must be Soul Exchange.

00:11:02.740 --> 00:11:04.840
But Ishizu knows that.

00:11:05.860 --> 00:11:07.840
Soul Exchange.

00:11:08.200 --> 00:11:11.400
Your next turn will end of the game.

00:11:13.080 --> 00:11:16.140
Just as I saw in my vision.

00:11:16.800 --> 00:11:18.720
My turn.  I draw.

00:11:20.780 --> 00:11:22.890
I set a card.

00:11:25.020 --> 00:11:26.780
Play whatever you like.

00:11:26.780 --> 00:11:29.500
But don't forget to summon a monster.

00:11:29.850 --> 00:11:33.430
Seto, the final trap will be the biggest.

00:11:33.640 --> 00:11:36.440
The trap card Sacrifice's Blast.

00:11:36.440 --> 00:11:41.880
When I placed this card on the field, a bomb was placed inside one of my monsters.

00:11:46.050 --> 00:11:51.250
If it's tributed to summon a monster, that monster will be destroyed when it attacks.

00:11:51.460 --> 00:11:53.360
Even if it's a God.

00:11:54.420 --> 00:11:56.400
I summon another monster!

00:11:59.180 --> 00:12:01.630
Ishizu now has all the monsters I need!

00:12:01.880 --> 00:12:05.620
How scary.  My sister is making this duel exciting.

00:12:05.620 --> 00:12:08.000
Almost too much.

00:12:09.140 --> 00:12:11.010
But is this a trap?

00:12:11.010 --> 00:12:14.080
What if Ishizu expects Soul Exchange?

00:12:16.280 --> 00:12:19.540
But my only choice is to bet on Obelisk!

00:12:19.850 --> 00:12:21.320
I activate my set card!

00:12:21.640 --> 00:12:24.090
Kelbek!  Agido!  Zolga!

00:12:24.090 --> 00:12:27.770
Ishizu, I'm tributing your monsters!

00:12:27.770 --> 00:12:29.510
I flip over my set card!

00:12:29.510 --> 00:12:31.150
Soul Exchange!

00:12:32.820 --> 00:12:33.960
I caught you.

00:12:37.200 --> 00:12:39.780
I'll let you see a God!

00:12:41.220 --> 00:12:44.810
Come!  Obelisk the Tormentor!

00:13:17.060 --> 00:13:18.790
He finally summoned it.

00:13:18.790 --> 00:13:20.560
Nice, big brother!

00:13:20.560 --> 00:13:23.800
This is Kaiba's God Card...

00:13:23.800 --> 00:13:25.380
Obelisk the Tormentor!

00:13:25.730 --> 00:13:31.150
Next turn, my God's attack will destroy the future you foretold!

00:13:33.080 --> 00:13:34.720
I end my turn.

00:13:35.230 --> 00:13:39.090
When Obelisk attacks, your role comes to an end.

00:13:39.430 --> 00:13:40.760
My turn!

00:13:41.240 --> 00:13:43.480
Attack me.

00:13:43.710 --> 00:13:45.320
Well, Ishizu?

00:13:45.540 --> 00:13:50.240
Obelisk - the God of Destruction - will annihilate you and bring me victory!

00:13:50.940 --> 00:13:54.680
The set card that was sent to the graveyard is an invisible trap.

00:13:54.680 --> 00:13:57.600
The trap activates when it's placed on the field.

00:13:57.860 --> 00:14:01.440
Seto, the trap has already been activated.

00:14:06.980 --> 00:14:11.560
Seto, you tributed Kelbek, Agito and Zolga.

00:14:11.560 --> 00:14:16.260
By tributing my monsters, my trap will destroy your monster.

00:14:16.960 --> 00:14:22.220
And you'll take damage equal to your destroyed monster's attack points.

00:14:24.530 --> 00:14:28.340
The trap triggers when Obelisk attacks.

00:14:28.560 --> 00:14:34.610
And you'll lose, just as my Millennium Necklace showed me.

00:14:34.610 --> 00:14:38.800
Ishizu, you have no monsters to defend with.

00:14:39.160 --> 00:14:41.290
I'll let you surrender.

00:14:43.920 --> 00:14:47.750
Yugi, do you think Kaiba will win?

00:14:47.750 --> 00:14:48.660
Yugi?

00:14:49.160 --> 00:14:52.450
Can he really defeat Ishizu with this attack?

00:14:52.450 --> 00:14:57.440
Why did Ishizu's Millennium Necklace show that Kaiba will lose?

00:14:57.700 --> 00:14:58.760
Yugi...

00:14:59.340 --> 00:15:01.280
I have a bad feeling.

00:15:07.220 --> 00:15:08.680
Well, Ishizu?

00:15:08.680 --> 00:15:11.460
Prepared to take God's attack?

00:15:11.720 --> 00:15:16.260
That's right.  Your only option is to attack with your God.

00:15:16.560 --> 00:15:18.920
Just as I saw in my vision.

00:15:21.160 --> 00:15:22.800
Go, God!

00:15:22.800 --> 00:15:28.000
When Obelisk attacks, Sacrifice's Blast activates.

00:15:28.540 --> 00:15:30.910
Obelisk the Tormentor!  Attack!

00:15:37.900 --> 00:15:38.580
What?

00:15:44.580 --> 00:15:46.680
That's your future.

00:15:46.680 --> 00:15:49.790
Now finish yourself.

00:15:50.040 --> 00:15:51.720
This match is over.

00:15:52.420 --> 00:15:56.360
As soon as Kaiba attacks...  Boom!

00:15:56.860 --> 00:15:59.940
My sister is truly frightening.

00:16:00.820 --> 00:16:01.770
Here I go!

00:16:01.770 --> 00:16:04.100
Obelisk the Tormentor!

00:16:04.100 --> 00:16:05.140
It's over.

00:16:06.560 --> 00:16:07.900
What?

00:16:11.780 --> 00:16:13.050
The Millennium Rod!

00:16:14.580 --> 00:16:15.150
Atta-

00:16:22.100 --> 00:16:24.170
Kaiba stopped his attack?

00:16:24.610 --> 00:16:26.110
What's wrong, Kaiba?

00:16:26.110 --> 00:16:27.030
Big brother!

00:16:38.480 --> 00:16:40.330
What's this?

00:16:45.910 --> 00:16:47.770
What's this vision?

00:16:48.200 --> 00:16:50.240
What's this sadness I feel?

00:16:52.040 --> 00:16:54.520
Why did he stop his attack?

00:16:55.040 --> 00:16:57.530
Is it due to the Millennium Rod?

00:17:03.510 --> 00:17:04.640
Kaiba...

00:17:06.860 --> 00:17:08.040
That tablet...

00:17:08.640 --> 00:17:11.370
It's Blue-Eyes White Dragon.

00:17:11.730 --> 00:17:14.210
Why am I seeing this?

00:17:15.020 --> 00:17:16.360
What's this?

00:17:22.270 --> 00:17:23.530
Blue-Eyes...

00:17:24.240 --> 00:17:26.810
What do you want me to do?

00:17:29.980 --> 00:17:32.330
I'll take this as a sign!

00:17:32.740 --> 00:17:35.260
I activate a spell card from my hand!

00:17:35.710 --> 00:17:37.170
Silent Doom!

00:17:37.170 --> 00:17:41.780
I summon Gadget Soldier from my graveyard in defense position!

00:17:43.500 --> 00:17:47.310
Impossible!  I didn't see this in my vision!

00:17:47.720 --> 00:17:52.750
To summon Blue-Eyes from my hand, I need to tribute two monsters.

00:17:52.960 --> 00:17:53.860
Therefore...

00:17:53.860 --> 00:17:54.860
No way!

00:17:54.860 --> 00:17:55.750
Yes!

00:17:55.750 --> 00:17:57.680
I tribute a God!

00:17:57.940 --> 00:17:59.170
What?

00:17:59.170 --> 00:18:00.170
Is he serious?

00:18:00.170 --> 00:18:01.440
Obelisk?

00:18:01.440 --> 00:18:02.620
Tribute?

00:18:02.820 --> 00:18:04.020
My pride...

00:18:04.320 --> 00:18:06.020
My soul...

00:18:06.570 --> 00:18:08.550
I decide my own future!

00:18:08.550 --> 00:18:11.060
Obelisk!  Gadget Soldier!

00:18:13.320 --> 00:18:16.200
Tribute yourselves for my servant!

00:18:16.860 --> 00:18:19.870
He tributed Obelisk?  A God?

00:18:20.080 --> 00:18:27.050
Ishizu, I'll show you my servant that represents my pride and soul!

00:18:27.280 --> 00:18:30.300
Come, Blue-Eyes White Dragon!

00:18:37.460 --> 00:18:40.230
The future has changed!

00:18:44.840 --> 00:18:46.110
Kaiba...

00:18:46.510 --> 00:18:48.430
What did you see?

00:18:48.840 --> 00:18:53.370
Seto, you truly are the master of the mythical white creature!

00:18:55.020 --> 00:18:59.680
Ishizu, did Blue-Eyes appear in your vision?

00:19:01.770 --> 00:19:03.570
Seems not.

00:19:04.380 --> 00:19:06.120
I lose.

00:19:06.120 --> 00:19:08.020
This is my future!

00:19:08.240 --> 00:19:10.000
Go!  Blue-Eyes!

00:19:16.000 --> 00:19:17.820
Open the way for my future!

00:19:17.820 --> 00:19:20.670
Burst Stream of Destruction!

00:19:31.520 --> 00:19:33.370
I win, Ishizu!

00:19:33.920 --> 00:19:36.180
The winner is Master Seto!

00:19:36.400 --> 00:19:37.900
Wow!

00:19:37.900 --> 00:19:41.590
You were as great as I believed you'd be!

00:19:41.850 --> 00:19:47.530
Kaiba, you showed me that the future isn't written for a duelist.

00:19:47.780 --> 00:19:51.600
But the master of the mythical white creature on the tablet...

00:19:51.600 --> 00:19:54.320
The Millennium Rod's glow...

00:19:54.680 --> 00:19:57.400
The God Cards choose who wields them.

00:19:57.400 --> 00:19:58.950
Who are you?

00:19:59.820 --> 00:20:01.470
Impressive, Seto.

00:20:01.780 --> 00:20:05.400
You're now the true owner of a God Card.

00:20:06.120 --> 00:20:07.550
But why?

00:20:08.000 --> 00:20:12.050
There's something that people should believe in beyond a God.

00:20:12.050 --> 00:20:14.590
And that's what I did.

00:20:14.590 --> 00:20:19.680
Seto, I gained something important in this duel.

00:20:20.000 --> 00:20:21.760
The light of hope.

00:20:22.960 --> 00:20:26.530
That wasn't in the future that the Millennium Necklace predicted.

00:20:27.060 --> 00:20:31.470
Even if I won, I had little chance of saving Marik.

00:20:32.150 --> 00:20:37.640
I was willing to risk my life for that sliver of hope.

00:20:37.950 --> 00:20:40.650
To win and save my brother.

00:20:42.100 --> 00:20:44.760
It's getting interesting.

00:20:45.360 --> 00:20:47.260
I lost.

00:20:47.480 --> 00:20:50.760
But I learned that you can change the future.

00:20:51.350 --> 00:20:56.190
And the people here have the power to save Marik.

00:20:58.650 --> 00:21:02.800
Seto, people can change the future?

00:21:04.000 --> 00:21:06.800
If you succumb to the future, there is no light.

00:21:14.570 --> 00:21:16.010
Big brother!

00:21:20.220 --> 00:21:23.350
Next, it's time to finish our fight.

00:21:23.820 --> 00:21:24.520
Yeah.

00:21:28.530 --> 00:21:33.060
I will believe in the future that I cannot see.

00:21:44.010 --> 00:21:47.530
With Kaiba's win, we have our four semifinalists.

00:21:47.530 --> 00:21:51.420
The Battle Ship flies toward the third duel arena.

00:21:51.420 --> 00:21:54.520
But there are too many casualties in this battle!

00:21:54.520 --> 00:21:56.680
Please tell me, Ishizu!

00:21:56.680 --> 00:22:00.220
Why is Marik trying to kill everyone?

00:22:00.220 --> 00:22:05.260
Ishizu begins to talk about Marik's past and the Ishtars' tragedy.

00:22:05.260 --> 00:22:08.640
Next time on Yu-Gi-Oh!:
Ishtar Family's Truth Revealed

00:22:08.640 --> 00:22:10.200
Duel, standby!

00:22:13.290 --> 00:22:21.170
The sun never sets
It rises forever

00:22:21.170 --> 00:22:30.140
Don't let a dream end as a dream

00:22:30.470 --> 00:22:35.110
The straight rail and harsh route

00:22:35.110 --> 00:22:39.080
Whether to go or not 
all of yourself

00:22:39.510 --> 00:22:47.050
I'm tired of counting on my fingers inside this cage

00:22:47.050 --> 00:22:50.620
Respect! Boys  Show me how you act tough

00:22:50.620 --> 00:22:55.390
Draw a map, even if it's sloppy

00:22:55.390 --> 00:23:05.500
And walk it without stopping

00:23:05.500 --> 00:23:13.110
The sun never sets
If I can be like you

00:23:13.340 --> 00:23:22.080
Create freedom by exceeding common ideas

00:23:22.080 --> 00:23:30.060
I want to trust myself
Sometimes I'll lose my way but

